128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The AWS Cost Optimization System is a cloud-native project that automatically monitors your AWS billing data, sends email alerts when your spending goes above a set limit, stores daily cost reports inside an Amazon S3 bucket, and displays all of that information through a professional Streamlit web dashboard. The dashboard is hosted on an AWS EC2 server and runs continuously using PM2, which means it stays online even after you disconnect from the terminal or restart the server. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The project uses AWS Lambda for automatic billing data collection, Amazon EventBridge to schedule the Lambda function daily, Amazon SNS for email alerts, Amazon S3 to store the reports, and AWS Cost Explorer to pull the actual billing data from your AWS account. The entire codebase is version-controlled using Git and GitHub, and the deployment follows a real-world DevOps workflow including CI/CD with GitHub Actions. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
